WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.816
Hello.

00:00:01.816 --> 00:00:03.949
Hello, good evening.

00:00:03.949 --> 00:00:06.744
I am Ismo, and yes, I am from Finland.

00:00:06.744 --> 00:00:10.381
Yay, yay, yay.

00:00:10.381 --> 00:00:12.397
I moved to America about a year ago,

00:00:12.397 --> 00:00:13.933
and it's been great,

00:00:13.933 --> 00:00:15.085
but I have to tell you that it took

00:00:15.085 --> 00:00:17.091
a long time to learn the things,

00:00:17.091 --> 00:00:19.149
like the small, subtle things.

00:00:19.149 --> 00:00:20.941
It took me a year to figure out

00:00:20.941 --> 00:00:21.774
that the correct answer to, "What's up?"

00:00:21.774 --> 00:00:23.024
is "What's up?"

00:00:33.528 --> 00:00:35.522
It took a long time, but now, I know.

00:00:35.522 --> 00:00:38.222
If somebody says, "What's up?"

00:00:38.222 --> 00:00:43.047
I just say, "What's up?"

00:00:45.713 --> 00:00:50.439
It feels wrong, like I feel
I'm not answering a question,

00:00:50.439 --> 00:00:54.896
but they are happy, so
I just keep doing it.

00:00:54.896 --> 00:00:56.434
It took me even longer than that

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:59.367
to finally learn that, "Can I help you?"

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:04.367
actually means, "Go away."

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.523
I'm always learning,
but I think the language

00:01:11.523 --> 00:01:13.241
still has been the most difficult part,

00:01:13.241 --> 00:01:15.099
'cause I studied English for years,

00:01:15.099 --> 00:01:16.720
and I thought I know English,

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.128
but then, I moved to America.

00:01:18.128 --> 00:01:21.250
Turns out, no.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:24.265
I didn't really know it, all the things.

00:01:24.265 --> 00:01:26.875
I think the hardest word to truly master

00:01:26.875 --> 00:01:28.708
has been the word ass.

00:01:29.896 --> 00:01:31.768
Ass.

00:01:31.768 --> 00:01:32.868
I thought it's really easy.

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:37.628
It means a butt, but no.

00:01:37.628 --> 00:01:39.648
Like, yeah, sometimes it can mean a butt,

00:01:39.648 --> 00:01:43.027
but that's just the tip of the ass-berg.

00:01:45.521 --> 00:01:47.560
There are so many
meanings to the word ass.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:50.067
I think it's the most
complicated word in English.

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:51.475
I've been trying to
write a whole dictionary

00:01:51.475 --> 00:01:53.837
about just ass.

00:01:53.837 --> 00:01:57.087
There's so many, for example, lazy ass.

00:01:58.783 --> 00:02:02.950
That means lazy.

00:02:04.737 --> 00:02:06.860
Like, "My lazy ass husband."

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:09.484
It's the same sentence without the ass.

00:02:14.453 --> 00:02:17.036
The ass is just optional there.

00:02:18.828 --> 00:02:23.127
And long-ass means long.

00:02:23.127 --> 00:02:26.710
Like a long-ass flight,
it's a long flight.

00:02:27.883 --> 00:02:29.067
But if you're gonna make it longer,

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:32.065
you're gonna add ass.

00:02:32.065 --> 00:02:35.723
My definite favorite one, a grown-ass man.

00:02:37.809 --> 00:02:40.710
It turns out it means a grown man.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:45.464
The entire man has grown,

00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:49.597
not only his ass.

00:02:49.597 --> 00:02:53.418
I learned that you can
add ass to anything,

00:02:53.418 --> 00:02:56.389
and then it sounds a little bit cooler.

00:02:56.389 --> 00:02:59.879
Like anything, "I just
bought this blue-ass shirt."

00:03:03.698 --> 00:03:06.090
"Well, thank you, that was
some good-ass meatballs."

00:03:08.606 --> 00:03:10.602
Anything, but you have to be careful,

00:03:10.602 --> 00:03:12.501
'cause sometimes, if you
add ass to something,

00:03:12.501 --> 00:03:14.932
it can actually reverse the meaning

00:03:14.932 --> 00:03:16.751
of the original word.

00:03:16.751 --> 00:03:18.501
For example, badass.

00:03:19.828 --> 00:03:23.214
That's good.

00:03:23.214 --> 00:03:26.332
Bad is bad, but badass is good.

00:03:26.332 --> 00:03:28.051
But not always.

00:03:28.051 --> 00:03:30.024
Like, dumbass is still dumb.

00:03:32.551 --> 00:03:33.384
How could you know?

00:03:33.384 --> 00:03:34.483
You have to know specifically

00:03:34.483 --> 00:03:36.030
which ones are flipped.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:39.336
And then there's the concept of your ass,

00:03:39.336 --> 00:03:42.995
and your ass, that means yourself.

00:03:42.995 --> 00:03:44.552
Like, "Move your ass!"

00:03:46.291 --> 00:03:49.664
That's like move everything.

00:03:49.664 --> 00:03:52.906
Move your ass and the rest
of your body and everything.

00:03:52.906 --> 00:03:55.230
If you have a car, that's
included in the ass.

00:03:56.819 --> 00:03:59.368
All of them, same direction, just move.

00:03:59.368 --> 00:04:01.925
So your ass means yourself
plus all you have,

00:04:01.925 --> 00:04:04.758
but my ass, my ass, that means no.

00:04:07.006 --> 00:04:09.841
If I say that, "Wow,
this car is really fast,"

00:04:09.841 --> 00:04:12.563
and you say, "Oh, fast, my ass."

00:04:15.894 --> 00:04:20.894
It means no, it's not fast.

00:04:23.602 --> 00:04:25.587
To make it even more complicated,

00:04:25.587 --> 00:04:27.170
ass can be divided.

00:04:28.115 --> 00:04:29.939
If you are an ass, that means

00:04:29.939 --> 00:04:31.880
that you are being stupid,

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:33.587
but if you're half-ass-

00:04:40.477 --> 00:04:42.675
Then, it means that you are

00:04:42.675 --> 00:04:46.801
not concentrating properly.

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:48.691
And if you go even smaller,

00:04:48.691 --> 00:04:49.524
if you are a piece of ass-
Then, you are beautiful.

00:04:49.524 --> 00:04:50.357
Thanks a lot.

